extraction_notes: |
  - Rifts Conversion Book One printed 74-76 (file p075-p077). No Palladium Fantasy row exists for the Bearman; the id carries the `rifts-` prefix batch 1 used, because a Palladium Fantasy conversion could later claim the plain id.
  - S.D.C. is "2D4x10 plus those gained from O.C.C. and physical skills", so it is a POOL BONUS rather than sdc_base. The book''s rule that 100 combined S.D.C./H.P. make one M.D.C. point (printed 74) is a natural ability, not an mdc pool: the Bearman is not an M.D.C. creature.
  - The Horror Factor save is "+1 at levels 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 8, 10, 12 and 14", stored as a level-one bonus plus nine at_level steps.
  - "Attacks Per Melee (Rifts): Two in addition to O.C.C. Hand to Hand skill and level" is a flat combat bonus of 2 attacks.
  - Bionic P.S. and the natural A.R. of 11 are prose: the app has no P.S. class key and no natural armor field.
  - Swimming, Climbing and Prowl are the page''s instinctive figures, granted at the printed percentages with no per-level growth because the book states none. Tracking and scent recognition stay natural abilities, not the catalog''s Track skills, because they are senses with their own ladders.
  - Languages are the "Skills of Note" at the printed percentages; Wolfen has no language row, so it is `Language: Other`. The 20% who speak Troll or Faerie at 50% are in the Dragonese note rather than granted, because it is a fifth of the race and an either-or.
  - occ_restrictions is read from the "Available O.C.C.s" line. "Any Palladium RPG Men of Arms" names another game''s occupations, so only the Rifts O.C.C.s are listed; an O.C.C. of the named kinds imported later is not covered until it is added. The three-physical-skill limit and the magic bar are prose restrictions.
  - Psionics: "Standard, same as humans", so no psionics block. Magic: none, and P.P.E. 3D6.
  - The section-wide rule on printed 74 - a new arrival from the Palladium World picks up the regional language and two Modern W.P.s within weeks, then three Rifts skills from Communications, Pilot (basic vehicles), Technical and W.P. Modern after 2D4+4 months or one level, and one more language or skill every two levels - applies to a character who came from Palladium rather than one raised on Rifts Earth. It is not stored; the survey carries it.
