# Bearman of the North

## Lore

Bearmen are huge, hulking man-beasts from the Palladium World: nine to ten feet of black or very dark brown fur, fang and muscle, with the look and the temper of an angry giant bear. Their origin is lost - a magical experiment gone wrong, or beings summoned during the Time of a Thousand Magicks - and the Bearmen themselves do not know. On Rifts Earth they are taken for Lone Star mutants, Coalition Ursa-Warriors or demonic monstrosities, and a Bearman dropped into that alien world is angrier and quicker to strike than ever.

For all their bullying they are neither savages nor wanton killers. They respect life and nature, rarely attack unprovoked, and would rather beat an antagonist into submission than murder him - though they take what they want. An estimated 100-200 roam the Canadian wilderness and another hundred the Rockies and northern United States, most as nomadic Wilderness Scouts; slavers and the Minions of Splugorth prize them as gladiators. Sweets and alcohol are their common vices, and a Bearman''s loyalty to a proven friend is said to exceed even his temper.

**Alignment:** Any, but often Aberrant, Anarchist and Unprincipled.

**Size:** 9 to 10 feet (2.7 to 3 m). **Weight:** 1200 to 1800 pounds (540 to 810 kg).

**Average Life Span:** 60 years.

**Habitat:** Wilderness and forested mountains, ideally a cool or cold climate.

## GM Notes

Bearmen trust nobody until the person has proven himself, and especially hate Bug Bears and Xiticix. Mutant canines and Dog Boys, Kankoran, Psi-Stalkers, Simvan, Lyn-Srial and Faerie Folk are the likeliest to be accepted. Large two-handed swords and tree-trunk clubs are their S.D.C. weapons of choice, and they adapt quickly to Vibro-Blades and heavy energy weapons - pump guns, grenade and rocket launchers, particle beam rifles, plasma ejectors and rail guns. They rarely wear armor at home, but on Rifts Earth take to loose, heavy M.D.C. armor such as the Crusader and Gladiator styles.
', 'published', 'data-script'
